title Caravan boot -- the declaration becomes running children
prompt Autonomous lap -- Kyri and Radiant first, REMEMBER, the itineraries, the newest recommends; Standfast on reds; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; rota one canon doc; send each finished increment
think Read KYRI and RADIANT_STYLE first, so the voice shaped the round from the first token; then REMEMBER, the newest three log rows, and the recommend line that named the crux -- a supervision loop that spawns its children FROM a roster
think Standfast pass first -- crux/REDS.md living rows 80, 83, 84, 85 and every prose note read closed; row 84's gitignore root verified on disk (line 70 whitelists /crux/, present), REDS #85 closed with a loom on the prior lap, so the line was clear for constructive work
think The gap the last six rings left open -- roster.rye derives the table from the document, yet the supervisor still had no way to START from it, and a spawn loop reading a hand-written list would smuggle the second source of truth right past every proof
think Chose the boot ring as the crux -- highest Lindy of the agent-doable rungs, since it closes the arc from a file on disk to running processes, and every later ring (a child exercising its region, the parity suite) stands on it
think Designed five checkable properties rather than one success -- coverage, order, fidelity, constancy across restart, and refusal before action -- so the ring proves what an operator actually needs to trust
think The seam is argv -- one grant crosses as one region:perm word in the same three-word grammar the document uses, so the child re-derives nothing and the parent's fidelity check is not self-confirming
think W xor X crosses by ABSENCE rather than by a later check -- a mask holding write beside execute has no word at all, so it cannot be spelled onto the wire, and rwx reads back as no mask
think Made Capability.name_slice and ChildSlot.label_slice pub in capabilities.rye -- the minimal accretion boot needed to read the derived table it spawns from
obs Witness GREEN on the first metal pass, so the RED path was proven before it was trusted -- rendering a read-only grant as rw made line_agrees abort at exit 134, in supervise_domain, AFTER the first child came up and BEFORE the widened line ever spawned; the sound file restored and rebuilt GREEN
obs The load-bearing negative is refusal before action -- wide_roster.bron is whole by every property verify reads and still past four children, so boot answers TooManyDomains with no process started; a half-booted system looks alive while what its children depend on was never started
obs Constancy is a property of the code rather than a habit -- the capability line is built once outside the restart loop and reused, so a child that falls comes back holding exactly what it held before
obs tame_style_check caught one compound assert on the first run (assert(!(writes and runs))) -- split to the named-bool idiom roster.rye already uses; bans clean after, width-check exit 0, living-docs lint GREEN, living-card ASCII GREEN
obs Rota item 23 read this lap -- the one-clock naming law; the stamp on this log and on the module version came from TZ=America/New_York date, never fabricated
loom witness=caravan_boot_witness children=3 grants_handed=6 restarts=1 red_exit=134
file caravan/boot.rye the boot ring -- one declaration on disk becomes one real child process per declared domain
file tools/caravan_boot_witness.rish the witness -- GREEN on metal over the worked example, the wide declaration, the rwx grammar, and an absent document
file caravan/capabilities.rye name_slice and label_slice published, the minimal accretion boot needs to read the derived table
file caravan/README.md the ladder gains its boot rung and the section naming why children are spawned from the document
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge refilled -- seven rings, the document that boots, and the next crux named
recommend keep-going -- next a child that EXERCISES a granted region rather than only naming it: a real shared buffer carried between virtualiser and client, an ungranted reach refused at the door. No key, no funds.
